# .semgrep-allowlist.txt — one semgrep rule-id per line to EXCLUDE from
# hooks/sast-scan.sh. Blank lines and `# ...` comments are ignored.
#
# Move to `.semgrep-allowlist.txt` at your project root when you have
# at least one confirmed false positive.
#
# Rule IDs come from semgrep output:
#     python.lang.security.audit.exec-use.exec-use
#     python.django.security.audit.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string
#
# Every entry deserves a comment explaining WHY it's allowlisted.
# A silently-suppressed rule is worse than no rule.

# Example — comment out to activate:
# python.lang.security.audit.exec-use.exec-use
#   Reason: internal DSL runner in scripts/dsl_runner.py; input is
#   never user-controlled; reviewed 2026-07-03 by security-reviewer.
